WEBVTT

1
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:10,208
<i>♪ As I step down from the train ♪</i>

2
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:16,715
<i>♪ And there to meet me is
my mama and papa ♪</i>

3
00:04:18,342 --> 00:04:22,845
<i>♪ And down the road I
look and there runs... ♪</i>

4
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:24,681
We're closed.

5
00:04:24,682 --> 00:04:28,268
<i>♪ Hair of gold and lips like cherries... ♪</i>

6
00:04:29,228 --> 00:04:30,853
Sir...

7
00:04:30,854 --> 00:04:32,022
You OK?

8
00:04:35,484 --> 00:04:37,027
Useless!

9
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,333
Hey, babe?

10
00:05:39,423 --> 00:05:40,966
- Is something wrong?
- No.

11
00:05:43,177 --> 00:05:44,303
Is everything OK?

12
00:05:45,179 --> 00:05:47,347
No, it's fine. Um...

13
00:05:48,766 --> 00:05:51,435
It's just been a while
since I've been back home.

14
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:53,603
OK.

15
00:05:53,604 --> 00:05:55,188
Yeah, I mean, I can...

16
00:05:55,189 --> 00:05:56,982
I can take time off and...

17
00:05:58,108 --> 00:06:00,026
maybe finally meet your family.

18
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:01,862
No, it's... it's all right.

19
00:06:05,199 --> 00:06:08,035
There's just some stuff
I gotta deal with.

20
00:06:08,994 --> 00:06:10,162
On my own.

21
00:06:11,997 --> 00:06:13,665
I'll be back as soon as I can.

22
00:06:16,627 --> 00:06:17,961
I promise.

23
00:06:22,174 --> 00:06:23,175
OK.

24
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:28,347
I still wanna
meet your brother.

25
00:06:30,224 --> 00:06:31,683
I'd like that too.

26
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:35,187
Hold still.

27
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:41,067
How do I look?

28
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:42,111
Pretty.

29
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:45,072
Where did you put your glasses?

30
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:49,910
Are you sleeping
with them on again?

31
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,079
You know...

32
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,915
you need these to see...

33
00:06:57,251 --> 00:06:58,627
my beautiful face.

34
00:06:59,795 --> 00:07:01,130
You wanna go wash up?

35
00:07:01,964 --> 00:07:03,006
- OK.
- And get ready?

36
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,211
Morning, Auntie.

37
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:43,963
Mind making Gracie's lunch?

38
00:07:43,964 --> 00:07:44,882
Mm.

39
00:07:45,883 --> 00:07:47,633
I'm late. Can you make sure...

40
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:50,762
I'll make sure
she gets to school. Clean.

41
00:07:51,597 --> 00:07:53,223
Thank you.

42
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:06,069
Wanna grab a coffee?

43
00:09:14,012 --> 00:09:15,389
Big brother.

44
00:09:19,935 --> 00:09:21,186
Come in.

45
00:09:30,279 --> 00:09:32,405
Keep watching that screen and

46
00:09:32,406 --> 00:09:34,032
your eyeballs will fall out.

47
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:37,411
Who are you?

48
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:41,039
I'm your relative. Mise'l.

49
00:09:43,292 --> 00:09:44,960
He's your uncle.

50
00:09:46,086 --> 00:09:47,753
Uncle.

51
00:09:47,754 --> 00:09:48,880
Come say hi.

52
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,760
Hi. I got this for you.

53
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:57,389
What do you say?

54
00:09:58,807 --> 00:10:01,310
- Thank you.
- Hey.

55
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:05,230
- Wanna pick out a bedtime story?
- OK.

56
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:12,612
Remember to brush your teeth,
OK?

57
00:10:18,827 --> 00:10:20,954
- Sit.
- Thank you.

58
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,463
She's huge.

59
00:10:31,006 --> 00:10:33,133
Yeah. Yeah, she is.

60
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:39,765
Where's <i>Nsukwis</i> Malia'n?

61
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:42,893
Oh, it's bingo night.

62
00:10:45,395 --> 00:10:47,814
Is, um... Bobby with you?

63
00:10:48,482 --> 00:10:49,483
Barry.

64
00:10:50,484 --> 00:10:52,486
No, it's just me.

65
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,203
So, what brought you
all the way out here?

66
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:08,919
You OK?

67
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,428
I saw him.

68
00:11:23,100 --> 00:11:25,477
I stopped by the old house
on the way over.

69
00:11:27,104 --> 00:11:28,563
Whole area is clear-cut.

70
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:34,777
They're gutting the forest.
If they make it to the cave...

71
00:11:34,778 --> 00:11:37,530
We both swore we'd never...
talk about this.

72
00:11:37,531 --> 00:11:40,617
If he can get to me in the city,
he's already at your backdoor.

73
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,664
We go in there...

74
00:11:46,665 --> 00:11:47,748
we take care of him,

75
00:11:47,749 --> 00:11:50,042
and we can both get back
to our own lives.

76
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,002
No.

77
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:52,963
No.

78
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:55,424
It's done.

79
00:11:56,508 --> 00:11:57,968
He's... gone.

80
00:11:58,885 --> 00:12:01,596
We both just...
need to let this go.

81
00:12:21,283 --> 00:12:23,493
He's not letting
either of us go.

82
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,122
I can't carry it alone.

83
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:45,723
Holy Mary.

84
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:48,768
- I must be seeing things.
- Hello, Auntie.

85
00:12:49,352 --> 00:12:51,770
Not been home in 20 years.

86
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:53,856
It hasn't been that long.

87
00:12:53,857 --> 00:12:57,110
Missed five funerals, barely
call or send a text message...

88
00:12:57,986 --> 00:13:00,988
And now you appear
just like that.

89
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,198
I'm sorry.

90
00:13:02,199 --> 00:13:03,824
Nothing to be afraid of.

91
00:13:03,825 --> 00:13:04,951
We're family.

92
00:13:08,205 --> 00:13:10,789
It's good to see you, <i>kwis.</i>

93
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,043
Even if you are
an ungrateful brat.

94
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,879
If you'd called ahead,

95
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,380
I could've cleaned out

96
00:13:18,381 --> 00:13:20,049
the spare room for you.

97
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:21,843
I'm not staying long.

98
00:13:22,886 --> 00:13:25,430
Dad, can I go and play outside?

99
00:13:26,973 --> 00:13:29,643
You can,
but stay out of the dirt.

100
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:37,650
Don't expect me
to go out of my way

101
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:39,611
to entertain you
while you're here.

102
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:42,780
Actually, I'm going camping

103
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:44,533
in the Old Forest.

104
00:13:51,498 --> 00:13:52,998
Hello?

105
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:56,961
No, I told you.
Don't listen to her...

106
00:13:56,962 --> 00:13:58,421
What are you doing?

107
00:13:59,256 --> 00:14:01,132
You know
you can't go in there alone.

108
00:14:02,342 --> 00:14:04,135
Someone has to.

109
00:14:06,096 --> 00:14:07,722
What? No...

110
00:14:14,312 --> 00:14:15,438
Antle?

111
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:19,734
What's she doing?

112
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:50,765
Grace!

113
00:14:54,728 --> 00:14:55,729
You all right?

114
00:14:57,814 --> 00:14:59,149
You have to aim.

115
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:03,902
What?

116
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,363
He said you have to aim.

117
00:15:10,744 --> 00:15:13,580
- Go back inside.
- But I want to play out here.

118
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:17,959
See if you can find that song
on YouTube for me.

119
00:15:42,359 --> 00:15:45,528
You never went back to
the woods after all these years?

120
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:47,947
Did you?

121
00:16:47,841 --> 00:16:49,134
- George?
- Yeah?

122
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:52,302
You noticed anything different
here lately?

123
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:54,596
Chief and Counsel were

124
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:56,683
asking me the same thing.

125
00:16:57,559 --> 00:16:59,519
Have you seen anything?

126
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:03,439
We're looking for a cave

127
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:05,274
deep in the old forest

128
00:17:05,275 --> 00:17:06,775
with petroglyphs

129
00:17:06,776 --> 00:17:08,194
carved into the entrance.

130
00:17:10,155 --> 00:17:11,197
Hm.

131
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,450
Wait here.

132
00:17:19,581 --> 00:17:24,169
Oh, Natalie printed those off
for me.

133
00:17:25,462 --> 00:17:30,048
That's your
great-great-grandfather.

134
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,927
Old Holy Joe,
they called him...

135
00:17:33,845 --> 00:17:37,891
because he wore
a big, hand-carved cross.

136
00:17:43,897 --> 00:17:46,024
The way up here is blocked.

137
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:50,987
A windstorm knocked down
some trees.

138
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:54,199
Best to follow the river.

139
00:17:55,617 --> 00:17:56,618
Oof.

140
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:06,294
I've kept this for you.

141
00:18:07,796 --> 00:18:10,173
A medicine bundle,
for your journey.

142
00:18:11,382 --> 00:18:12,925
Thanks.

143
00:18:12,926 --> 00:18:15,303
The forest will reveal
the rest.

144
00:18:19,891 --> 00:18:21,059
Hm.

145
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,355
Thanks, guys.

146
00:18:28,066 --> 00:18:29,275
We should go.

147
00:18:30,026 --> 00:18:31,653
Thank you, Elder.

148
00:18:52,507 --> 00:18:54,425
So, you're a healer now?

149
00:18:57,428 --> 00:18:59,264
Mess off!

150
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:02,851
Fine. Keep all that shit
to yourself, then.

151
00:19:08,398 --> 00:19:09,482
Shit!

152
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:12,943
You all right?

153
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,737
Let's get this shit over with.

154
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:49,063
<i>Long ago, before disruption,</i>

155
00:19:49,898 --> 00:19:51,900
<i>the forest was
our first teacher.</i>

156
00:19:53,276 --> 00:19:56,863
<i>It gave us everything
we needed.</i>

157
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:01,200
<i>The people and the land are
forever related.</i>

158
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:09,500
<i>When the land is in pain,
so are we.</i>

159
00:20:11,878 --> 00:20:17,050
<i>In difficult times, we return
to the heart of the forest.</i>

160
00:20:20,345 --> 00:20:24,431
<i>We return to learn,</i>

161
00:20:24,432 --> 00:20:28,019
<i>and to be given
what is needed to heal.</i>

162
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:17,694
You got it going.

163
00:23:32,954 --> 00:23:34,247
We should stop here.

164
00:23:34,872 --> 00:23:37,333
The faster we get there,
the faster we get back.

165
00:23:48,344 --> 00:23:50,596
- Keep paddling.
- We're stopping!

166
00:23:51,597 --> 00:23:54,016
Help me find a place to land.

167
00:23:55,393 --> 00:23:57,228
Let's find a spot over there.

168
00:24:00,148 --> 00:24:02,316
Antle!

169
00:24:08,531 --> 00:24:09,532
Antle?

170
00:24:11,909 --> 00:24:12,952
Antle?

171
00:24:22,587 --> 00:24:24,172
I got you.

172
00:24:58,873 --> 00:24:59,957
We're safe.

173
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,668
It won't come now.

174
00:25:13,679 --> 00:25:15,348
He was chasing us again.

175
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:20,310
He wanted me to hold down Andy

176
00:25:20,311 --> 00:25:22,063
while he used the belt on him.

177
00:25:26,984 --> 00:25:28,194
I remember.

178
00:25:34,242 --> 00:25:35,201
What happens?

179
00:25:35,993 --> 00:25:37,536
After this?

180
00:25:38,496 --> 00:25:39,747
We survive.

181
00:26:58,451 --> 00:26:59,452
So...

182
00:27:00,286 --> 00:27:01,537
the canoe's gone.

183
00:27:02,204 --> 00:27:03,872
What's your big plan now?

184
00:27:03,873 --> 00:27:05,623
We're gonna walk the rest.

185
00:27:05,624 --> 00:27:08,543
- We're lost.
- We'll follow the river.

186
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:10,379
'Follow the river.'

187
00:27:12,089 --> 00:27:15,926
Assuming ghouls don't travel
on land too, of course.

188
00:27:19,889 --> 00:27:21,973
Grace will be fine.

189
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:23,600
How do you know that?

190
00:27:23,601 --> 00:27:24,977
<i>Nsukwis</i> has got her.

191
00:27:28,981 --> 00:27:31,901
Don't act like you suddenly
give a shit about my life.

192
00:27:32,985 --> 00:27:34,070
All right?

193
00:28:00,221 --> 00:28:01,430
What the fuck?

194
00:28:35,506 --> 00:28:37,133
Antle!

195
00:28:41,512 --> 00:28:43,388
Back away into the water...

196
00:28:43,389 --> 00:28:45,516
...slowly.

197
00:29:03,909 --> 00:29:05,995
Keep going, don't stop!

198
00:29:37,526 --> 00:29:39,737
You manage to salvage anything?

199
00:29:40,696 --> 00:29:41,614
Nope.

200
00:29:42,406 --> 00:29:44,241
Now everything's soaked again.

201
00:30:04,261 --> 00:30:05,638
Leech.

202
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:25,449
Remember when you fell
in a nest of leeches?

203
00:30:28,202 --> 00:30:29,119
What?

204
00:30:30,538 --> 00:30:31,664
The leech thing.

205
00:30:33,624 --> 00:30:37,252
They were everywhere.
It was like a wiggling...

206
00:30:37,253 --> 00:30:38,295
Mise'l!

207
00:30:39,213 --> 00:30:41,006
I'm just saying,
maybe this is then.

208
00:30:54,728 --> 00:30:56,313
It's just a worm.

209
00:30:57,523 --> 00:30:58,816
Pull back like this...

210
00:30:59,525 --> 00:31:00,776
then let go.

211
00:31:12,329 --> 00:31:13,413
If I catch a fish,

212
00:31:13,414 --> 00:31:15,290
- can you clean it?
- Nope.

213
00:31:15,291 --> 00:31:16,292
That's your job.

214
00:31:18,419 --> 00:31:20,337
- But I'll help you.
- OK.

215
00:31:23,841 --> 00:31:26,634
I saw you and Trevor
behind the house yesterday.

216
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:28,679
- What?
- You kissed him.

217
00:31:29,513 --> 00:31:31,472
- You're hurting me!
- Tell no one.

218
00:31:31,473 --> 00:31:33,391
- Let go!
- I'm serious.

219
00:31:33,392 --> 00:31:35,102
Swear to me you won't tell him.

220
00:31:37,438 --> 00:31:38,814
Antle!

221
00:31:41,358 --> 00:31:43,611
Will you help me gut my fish?

222
00:31:44,987 --> 00:31:46,947
You gotta catch one first,
dummy.

223
00:31:48,824 --> 00:31:52,160
Why were you kissing Trevor?
His sister likes you.

224
00:31:52,161 --> 00:31:53,704
And I like Trevor.

225
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:58,834
Come on.
Hurry up or he'll be pissed!

226
00:32:05,633 --> 00:32:08,969
<i>♪ Down the road I look
and there runs Mary ♪</i>

227
00:32:09,803 --> 00:32:13,556
<i>♪ Hair of gold and
lips like cherries ♪</i>

228
00:32:13,557 --> 00:32:19,938
<i>♪ It's good to touch the
green, green grass of home ♪</i>

229
00:32:21,357 --> 00:32:26,277
<i>♪ Yes, they'll all come
to meet me ♪</i>

230
00:32:26,278 --> 00:32:30,114
<i>♪ Arms reaching, smiling sweetly ♪</i>

231
00:32:30,115 --> 00:32:33,284
<i>♪ It's so good to touch... ♪</i>

232
00:32:33,285 --> 00:32:34,787
No, Mise'l!

233
00:33:24,128 --> 00:33:26,714
You know, I remember that day.

234
00:33:35,139 --> 00:33:37,266
Always jealous of your bike.

235
00:33:38,976 --> 00:33:41,478
The pink monster I inherited
from Cousin Dawn?

236
00:33:45,149 --> 00:33:47,108
It had brakes
on the handle bars.

237
00:33:47,109 --> 00:33:47,985
Yeah.

238
00:33:49,903 --> 00:33:52,614
I got the shit kicked out of me
at least three times.

239
00:33:58,120 --> 00:33:59,246
It had a bell too.

240
00:34:09,882 --> 00:34:11,967
I don't know
why I can't be like that...

241
00:34:13,427 --> 00:34:15,387
that kid anymore.

242
00:34:17,139 --> 00:34:18,307
You know?

243
00:34:22,186 --> 00:34:23,145
Yeah.

244
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:26,148
I know.

245
00:34:48,629 --> 00:34:51,256
Push!

246
00:34:54,009 --> 00:34:54,968
Push!

247
00:34:57,805 --> 00:34:59,348
Do you speak our language?

248
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:02,142
We speak it.

249
00:35:04,895 --> 00:35:06,814
I'm Mise'l.
This is my brother.

250
00:35:07,773 --> 00:35:10,191
- His name is Antle.
- Mm.

251
00:35:10,192 --> 00:35:12,401
I'm Holy Joe.

252
00:35:12,402 --> 00:35:13,778
I was praying for help.

253
00:35:13,779 --> 00:35:15,404
Looks like the Lord sent you.

254
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:17,074
Can you lend a hand?

255
00:35:21,995 --> 00:35:24,790
We'll rest after, have a meal.

256
00:35:25,541 --> 00:35:27,333
You're both welcome to join.

257
00:35:27,334 --> 00:35:29,086
Thank you.

258
00:35:38,178 --> 00:35:39,680
Push!

259
00:35:46,395 --> 00:35:47,813
Push, push!

260
00:35:49,439 --> 00:35:50,691
Push, push!

261
00:35:53,193 --> 00:35:54,695
Hey!

262
00:35:58,365 --> 00:35:59,825
Good job, <i>kwis</i>.

263
00:36:00,576 --> 00:36:02,618
<i>Bless us, O Lord,</i>

264
00:36:02,619 --> 00:36:04,830
<i>and the gifts we are about
to receive from Thy bounty,</i>

265
00:36:06,081 --> 00:36:08,082
through Christ our Lord.

266
00:36:08,083 --> 00:36:09,167
Amen.

267
00:36:11,753 --> 00:36:14,339
Can't say I've seen
this cave of yours.

268
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:16,758
This place is tricky.

269
00:36:18,010 --> 00:36:21,054
Been using these roads
for the past 20 years now.

270
00:36:21,889 --> 00:36:23,515
Seen all sorts of things.

271
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:26,350
I don't know how to find it,

272
00:36:26,351 --> 00:36:28,562
but I know someone
who can guide you.

273
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:30,897
Head west.

274
00:36:30,898 --> 00:36:33,066
A healer lives there.

275
00:36:35,485 --> 00:36:37,321
Deep up in them hills.

276
00:36:38,864 --> 00:36:40,365
You go past the river,

277
00:36:41,074 --> 00:36:42,909
about a day or two.

278
00:36:42,910 --> 00:36:44,620
Look for the doorway.

279
00:36:48,665 --> 00:36:51,335
Sometimes it takes one spirit
to fight another.

280
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:54,546
Lord protect you.

281
00:36:59,134 --> 00:37:02,721
We're heading out
first thing in the morning.

282
00:37:03,722 --> 00:37:07,100
Eat. Rest.

283
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,522
Pray.

284
00:38:21,133 --> 00:38:22,968
Begone, spirit!

285
00:38:28,348 --> 00:38:30,850
<i>Ju'kwa'tik nuluksk.</i>

286
00:38:30,851 --> 00:38:33,061
<i>Come, my nephews.</i>

287
00:38:34,521 --> 00:38:36,897
<i>Ke wi'je'wi</i>.

288
00:38:36,898 --> 00:38:38,567
<i>Walk with me.</i>

289
00:38:51,204 --> 00:38:53,206
<i>Wel-jesi-oq te't.</i>

290
00:38:54,166 --> 00:38:55,917
<i>You're safe here.</i>

291
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:15,811
<i>Te't na naka'si'te'sk</i>

292
00:39:15,812 --> 00:39:18,106
<i>t'et klapis...</i>

293
00:39:18,940 --> 00:39:21,860
<i>This is where my
path one day ends.</i>

294
00:39:29,409 --> 00:39:32,746
<i>Kilo nasik si'eow wa'sioq...</i>

295
00:39:34,206 --> 00:39:36,875
<i>But your path continues.</i>

296
00:40:19,376 --> 00:40:22,586
<i>Amu'jpa ma'ja'sioq</i>

297
00:40:22,587 --> 00:40:25,590
<i>aqq kesalulo'q</i>

298
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:29,344
<i>It's time for you to go.</i>

299
00:43:20,974 --> 00:43:21,891
Antle!

300
00:43:23,184 --> 00:43:24,477
Let's rest a minute.

301
00:43:38,742 --> 00:43:41,411
I remember when I was the one
who used to help you up.

302
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,216
Job keeps you in shape.

303
00:43:58,678 --> 00:44:01,556
Never know when you need
to carry a 200-pound guy.

304
00:44:02,557 --> 00:44:05,685
I am not a guy.
Or 200 pounds.

305
00:44:09,522 --> 00:44:10,940
201. Sorry.

306
00:44:18,490 --> 00:44:20,200
Grace seems pretty happy.

307
00:44:22,077 --> 00:44:24,245
Probably not easy
raising a kid alone.

308
00:44:28,958 --> 00:44:30,794
<i>Nsukwis</i> helps.

309
00:44:32,253 --> 00:44:33,838
Still, it's hard.

310
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:38,676
Explains why you never got out.

311
00:44:41,262 --> 00:44:43,223
What the hell is
that supposed to mean?

312
00:44:45,809 --> 00:44:47,477
Do you really wanna stay here?

313
00:44:49,979 --> 00:44:51,815
You've got your life
in the city.

314
00:44:53,858 --> 00:44:55,110
I've got mine here.

315
00:44:55,944 --> 00:44:57,237
What about Grace?

316
00:44:58,446 --> 00:45:00,240
What kind of life
will she have?

317
00:45:06,621 --> 00:45:09,081
I got my shit together,
all right.

318
00:45:09,082 --> 00:45:10,333
I'm not some weak little f...

319
00:46:37,879 --> 00:46:39,047
Wait.

320
00:46:46,137 --> 00:46:47,180
Mise'l?

321
00:46:50,934 --> 00:46:52,393
Calm down.

322
00:46:54,312 --> 00:46:55,897
Listen to me.

323
00:46:57,565 --> 00:46:59,484
It'll be fine, don't cry.

324
00:47:02,320 --> 00:47:04,531
It's OK. You're OK.

325
00:47:05,281 --> 00:47:07,742
We won't tell anyone,
I promise.

326
00:47:09,035 --> 00:47:11,079
You didn't do anything wrong.

327
00:47:22,298 --> 00:47:23,550
I'm sorry.

328
00:47:26,094 --> 00:47:27,594
About earlier.

329
00:47:27,595 --> 00:47:29,264
I don't think that about you.

330
00:47:33,726 --> 00:47:36,521
Come on. This way.

331
00:47:54,581 --> 00:47:57,083
No respect for property.

332
00:48:10,179 --> 00:48:12,557
Help! Fire, fire!

333
00:48:30,033 --> 00:48:31,784
Fuck!

334
00:48:32,994 --> 00:48:34,162
Antle!

335
00:48:49,052 --> 00:48:50,470
I knew I heard something.

336
00:48:55,099 --> 00:48:57,935
- Indian?
- Half-breed maybe?

337
00:48:59,479 --> 00:49:01,730
All these savages
dress strange.

338
00:49:01,731 --> 00:49:04,316
Ha! Let's bring him in.

339
00:49:04,317 --> 00:49:05,817
Better to scalp him.

340
00:49:05,818 --> 00:49:07,612
Ten whole Guineas.

341
00:49:20,958 --> 00:49:22,627
Come, help me!

342
00:49:30,885 --> 00:49:33,261
- You're Mi'kmaw?
- Yes.

343
00:49:33,262 --> 00:49:35,056
Are you spirits?

344
00:49:36,891 --> 00:49:39,184
We're safe here for now.

345
00:49:39,185 --> 00:49:42,396
They couldn't find their nose
in front of their face.

346
00:49:42,397 --> 00:49:44,565
My brother is sick.

347
00:49:59,414 --> 00:50:03,292
Whatever made you sick
is eating you from the inside.

348
00:50:04,085 --> 00:50:05,336
You too.

349
00:50:09,674 --> 00:50:12,176
We're looking for a healer.

350
00:50:14,137 --> 00:50:16,138
It's too risky.

351
00:50:16,139 --> 00:50:17,556
They look strange,

352
00:50:17,557 --> 00:50:20,017
but they are like us.

353
00:50:20,643 --> 00:50:22,854
We can't abandon them.

354
00:50:23,646 --> 00:50:25,480
Just tell us where to go.

355
00:50:25,481 --> 00:50:26,523
I'll take you.

356
00:50:26,524 --> 00:50:28,025
Hey.

357
00:50:28,693 --> 00:50:31,070
No, I can't lose you.

358
00:50:31,904 --> 00:50:34,449
I'll be quick.

359
00:50:38,870 --> 00:50:42,749
I can't take you all the way,
just past the battlefield.

360
00:50:45,209 --> 00:50:46,419
Thank you.

361
00:50:52,341 --> 00:50:53,885
Come on!

362
00:50:55,928 --> 00:50:57,430
Let's go.

363
00:51:13,362 --> 00:51:15,655
Keep heading west.

364
00:51:15,656 --> 00:51:18,284
Follow the river.
She'll find you.

365
00:51:19,702 --> 00:51:20,953
We'll meet again.

366
00:51:53,986 --> 00:51:56,531
Probably not even out there.

367
00:51:59,617 --> 00:52:02,495
Hear that?
Come back this way.

368
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:09,961
Antle!

369
00:52:20,513 --> 00:52:22,597
Maybe something...

370
00:52:22,598 --> 00:52:24,725
Maybe something in here
will help.

371
00:52:32,358 --> 00:52:34,402
You promised
everything would be OK.

372
00:54:02,448 --> 00:54:04,742
Long have I waited.

373
00:54:45,992 --> 00:54:48,201
It's been so long

374
00:54:48,202 --> 00:54:49,203
since I've seen you both.

375
00:54:55,876 --> 00:54:57,878
Welcome, Father.

376
00:55:05,469 --> 00:55:06,929
Gracie?

377
00:55:17,148 --> 00:55:19,400
Don't mind them.

378
00:55:22,945 --> 00:55:25,406
We're safe here.

379
00:55:29,952 --> 00:55:32,246
How long have you been here?

380
00:55:34,373 --> 00:55:35,749
This is the place of spirits.

381
00:55:35,750 --> 00:55:37,543
Time is unfixed.

382
00:55:43,883 --> 00:55:46,052
You'll need this
for what's to come.

383
00:55:49,263 --> 00:55:51,766
We won't come back, will we?

384
00:55:54,310 --> 00:55:58,355
In my season of time,
you never return.

385
00:56:08,240 --> 00:56:10,284
They're coming.

386
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:19,418
Don't look back, don't stop.

387
00:56:21,837 --> 00:56:23,255
Don't look back.

388
00:56:26,342 --> 00:56:28,135
I know what you intend to do.

389
00:56:29,804 --> 00:56:31,721
But this...

390
00:56:31,722 --> 00:56:33,432
you can't stop it.

391
00:56:34,016 --> 00:56:35,767
<i>Wkamlamun.</i>

392
00:56:35,768 --> 00:56:37,061
It's the heart.

393
00:56:39,230 --> 00:56:42,775
The place where you're going,
there's a large lake nearby.

394
00:56:43,609 --> 00:56:46,487
Carved by glaciers,
thousands of times.

395
00:56:48,114 --> 00:56:50,031
Return him to the land there.

396
00:56:50,032 --> 00:56:52,033
I've prepared the way.

397
00:56:52,034 --> 00:56:53,202
Come with us.

398
00:56:54,662 --> 00:56:57,123
When it's all over,
we can go home.

399
00:56:57,998 --> 00:56:59,792
- All together.
- Mm.

400
00:57:01,460 --> 00:57:03,087
All of us.

401
00:57:12,471 --> 00:57:14,598
You have to go now,
or you'll miss it.

402
00:57:31,323 --> 00:57:32,658
You're so beautiful.

403
00:57:36,912 --> 00:57:38,998
Come home this time.

404
00:58:28,214 --> 00:58:29,340
Mise'l.

405
00:58:30,466 --> 00:58:31,842
I can't.

406
00:58:37,640 --> 00:58:38,682
I can't.

407
01:00:17,865 --> 01:00:21,577
<i>♪ As I step down from the train ♪</i>

408
01:00:22,286 --> 01:00:28,500
<i>♪ And there to meet me is
my mama and papa ♪</i>

409
01:00:30,502 --> 01:00:35,966
<i>♪ Down the road I look
and there runs Mary ♪</i>

410
01:00:36,675 --> 01:00:40,428
<i>♪ Hair of gold and
lips like cherries ♪</i>

411
01:00:40,429 --> 01:00:46,894
<i>♪ It's good to touch the
green, green grass of home ♪</i>

412
01:00:48,145 --> 01:00:52,691
<i>♪ Yes, they'll all come to meet me ♪</i>

413
01:00:53,400 --> 01:00:57,071
<i>♪ Arms reaching, smiling sweetly ♪</i>

414
01:00:58,238 --> 01:01:04,953
<i>♪ It's so good to touch the
green, green grass of home ♪</i>

415
01:01:06,205 --> 01:01:10,042
<i>♪ The old house is still standing ♪</i>

416
01:01:10,751 --> 01:01:13,587
<i>♪ Though the paint... ♪</i>

417
01:01:36,110 --> 01:01:37,569
<i>♪ ...The green, green grass ♪</i>

418
01:02:05,764 --> 01:02:06,849
Get out.

419
01:02:42,718 --> 01:02:43,886
Get my gun.

420
01:02:47,890 --> 01:02:48,932
Not you.

421
01:02:50,893 --> 01:02:52,019
My son.

422
01:03:50,577 --> 01:03:51,787
Come here.

423
01:03:54,873 --> 01:03:57,042
Don't drop it, you little shit.

424
01:04:33,829 --> 01:04:35,538
Barrel.

425
01:04:35,539 --> 01:04:36,582
Butt.

426
01:04:37,207 --> 01:04:38,333
Trigger.

427
01:04:51,680 --> 01:04:53,015
You aim this

428
01:04:53,724 --> 01:04:55,100
at what needs shooting,

429
01:04:56,268 --> 01:04:57,561
breathe out...

430
01:04:59,521 --> 01:05:01,064
and squeeze gently.

431
01:05:02,190 --> 01:05:03,734
You understand?

432
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:11,658
Aim at the bottle.

433
01:05:13,285 --> 01:05:14,661
Breathe out.

434
01:05:19,541 --> 01:05:20,751
And squeeze.

435
01:05:46,068 --> 01:05:47,235
Walk.

436
01:05:51,490 --> 01:05:52,991
Walk, boy.

437
01:05:57,996 --> 01:05:59,581
And don't look back.

438
01:06:13,970 --> 01:06:15,722
We're gonna play a little game.

439
01:06:17,099 --> 01:06:18,725
Shoot the fruit.

440
01:06:23,271 --> 01:06:24,398
Remember.

441
01:06:26,775 --> 01:06:27,818
Aim...

442
01:06:29,486 --> 01:06:33,239
breathe out and squeeze.

443
01:06:33,240 --> 01:06:34,574
- But...
- Do it!

444
01:06:38,578 --> 01:06:39,871
Do. It.

445
01:06:48,797 --> 01:06:49,881
Do it.

446
01:06:56,638 --> 01:06:58,014
- Do it!
- No!

447
01:07:03,937 --> 01:07:06,523
Oh, shit!
You shot him!

448
01:07:10,026 --> 01:07:11,611
Come with me.

449
01:07:42,434 --> 01:07:43,727
Little bro.

450
01:07:46,938 --> 01:07:48,815
You ready for what's next?

451
01:09:39,551 --> 01:09:41,136
Take him to the river.

452
01:11:29,744 --> 01:11:32,330
Where's... the skull?

453
01:12:09,200 --> 01:12:10,744
I'll go.

454
01:13:32,659 --> 01:13:34,035
Aim.

455
01:13:34,953 --> 01:13:36,578
<i>Breathe...</i>

456
01:13:36,579 --> 01:13:37,622
<i>out.</i>

457
01:13:38,414 --> 01:13:39,749
<i>Do it.</i>

458
01:13:41,668 --> 01:13:43,002
<i>Squeeze.</i>

459
01:13:53,930 --> 01:13:55,014
Please.

460
01:14:04,774 --> 01:14:06,317
<i>Do it!</i>

461
01:14:59,913 --> 01:15:01,372
<i>I know...</i>

462
01:15:02,498 --> 01:15:04,709
<i>it's hard for you...</i>

463
01:15:06,920 --> 01:15:08,713
to be around me.

464
01:15:15,970 --> 01:15:17,555
It's true.

465
01:15:28,316 --> 01:15:30,651
I knew it the day
you left me behind

466
01:15:30,652 --> 01:15:32,111
for the big city.

467
01:15:35,657 --> 01:15:37,158
No, brother.

468
01:15:42,080 --> 01:15:44,499
I left because...

469
01:15:53,132 --> 01:15:54,550
I left because...

470
01:15:58,763 --> 01:16:00,890
every time you looked at me...

471
01:16:05,979 --> 01:16:07,689
all I saw was pain...

472
01:16:09,649 --> 01:16:10,775
and guilt.

473
01:16:13,736 --> 01:16:15,655
I didn't want that
to be your life.

474
01:16:24,414 --> 01:16:27,917
Leaving... didn't change that.

475
01:16:31,838 --> 01:16:33,756
<i>I wish we both could be different,</i>

476
01:16:34,757 --> 01:16:36,884
<i>everything could be different.</i>

477
01:22:39,121 --> 01:22:41,957
I knew you'd come home.

478
01:23:26,669 --> 01:23:28,713
<i>♪ Take my hand ♪</i>

479
01:23:29,296 --> 01:23:31,799
<i>♪ Walk with me ♪</i>

480
01:23:33,509 --> 01:23:37,346
<i>♪ Together you and I ♪</i>

481
01:23:39,390 --> 01:23:41,767
<i>♪ Always remember ♪</i>

482
01:23:42,810 --> 01:23:47,106
<i>♪ Sweetheart ♪</i>

483
01:23:48,023 --> 01:23:52,486
<i>♪ I will always be there for you ♪</i>

484
01:23:53,487 --> 01:23:58,743
<i>♪ Weya heya, heya heyo ♪</i>

485
01:24:00,870 --> 01:24:06,792
<i>♪ I would walk through the night ♪</i>

486
01:24:07,835 --> 01:24:11,505
<i>♪ Across the land to sea ♪</i>

487
01:24:14,049 --> 01:24:16,677
<i>♪ And see you standing there ♪</i>

488
01:24:17,261 --> 01:24:21,140
<i>♪ In new light ♪</i>

489
01:24:22,349 --> 01:24:24,976
<i>♪ Take my hand ♪</i>

490
01:24:24,977 --> 01:24:26,437
<i>♪ Walk with me ♪</i>

491
01:24:27,104 --> 01:24:33,359
<i>♪ Into new love ♪</i>

492
01:24:33,360 --> 01:24:36,655
<i>♪ New love ♪</i>

493
01:24:37,823 --> 01:24:43,370
<i>♪ Where we've been waiting ♪</i>

494
01:24:45,372 --> 01:24:51,879
<i>♪ Working towards our new love ♪</i>

495
01:24:54,632 --> 01:24:59,177
<i>♪ New love ♪</i>

496
01:24:59,178 --> 01:25:03,349
<i>♪ Oh will you wait ♪</i>

497
01:25:04,600 --> 01:25:08,604
<i>♪ Or walk with me? ♪</i>

498
01:25:12,274 --> 01:25:14,859
<i>♪ Take my hand ♪</i>

499
01:25:14,860 --> 01:25:19,239
<i>♪ And try to see ♪</i>

500
01:25:19,240 --> 01:25:22,535
<i>♪ Cross rivers that you've feared ♪</i>

501
01:25:25,037 --> 01:25:27,831
<i>♪ Stories you're afraid to hear ♪</i>

502
01:25:27,832 --> 01:25:32,169
<i>♪ Can't keep our love away ♪</i>

503
01:25:33,796 --> 01:25:39,425
<i>♪ I will always be there for you ♪</i>

504
01:25:39,426 --> 01:25:45,099
<i>♪ When you feel all this grief ♪</i>

505
01:25:46,267 --> 01:25:50,229
<i>♪ When your tears find you again ♪</i>

506
01:25:52,314 --> 01:25:55,567
<i>♪ When your heart asks who's there ♪</i>

507
01:25:55,568 --> 01:25:58,028
<i>♪ Dreams still whispering ♪</i>

508
01:25:59,196 --> 01:26:05,411
<i>♪ Until we start to sing again ♪</i>

509
01:26:06,036 --> 01:26:11,333
<i>♪ Weya heya, heya heyo ♪</i>

510
01:26:14,003 --> 01:26:16,088
<i>♪ Take my hand ♪</i>

511
01:26:16,714 --> 01:26:20,009
<i>♪ But not my light ♪</i>

512
01:26:21,051 --> 01:26:24,471
<i>♪ The words that we find are new ♪</i>

513
01:26:26,807 --> 01:26:28,892
<i>♪ And all of the ghosts ♪</i>

514
01:26:28,893 --> 01:26:33,772
<i>♪ That we sing back to ♪</i>

515
01:26:35,357 --> 01:26:39,320
<i>♪ Teach us our way of listening ♪</i>

516
01:26:41,238 --> 01:26:46,410
<i>♪ Give yourself to dancing days ♪</i>

517
01:26:47,494 --> 01:26:51,790
<i>♪ Sorrow and grief create a place ♪</i>

518
01:26:53,584 --> 01:26:56,503
<i>♪ For new love to enter ♪</i>

519
01:26:57,254 --> 01:27:00,758
<i>♪ If you listen for its name ♪</i>

520
01:27:02,301 --> 01:27:07,055
<i>♪ I will always be there for you ♪</i>

521
01:27:07,056 --> 01:27:12,853
<i>♪ In new love ♪</i>

522
01:27:13,520 --> 01:27:16,899
<i>♪ New love ♪</i>

523
01:27:18,067 --> 01:27:24,113
<i>♪ Where we've been waiting ♪</i>

524
01:27:24,114 --> 01:27:29,202
<i>♪ Walking towards ♪</i>

525
01:27:29,203 --> 01:27:34,041
<i>♪ New love ♪</i>

526
01:27:34,708 --> 01:27:38,629
<i>♪ New love ♪</i>

527
01:27:39,296 --> 01:27:44,175
<i>♪ Oh, will you wait ♪</i>

528
01:27:44,176 --> 01:27:49,390
<i>♪ Or walk with me? ♪</i>

529
01:27:53,894 --> 01:27:56,521
<i>♪ Take my hand ♪</i>

530
01:27:56,522 --> 01:27:58,857
<i>♪ Walk with me ♪</i>

531
01:28:00,859 --> 01:28:03,612
<i>♪ Together you and I ♪</i>

532
01:28:06,991 --> 01:28:10,243
<i>♪ Always remember ♪</i>

533
01:28:10,244 --> 01:28:14,206
<i>♪ Sweetheart ♪</i>

534
01:28:15,249 --> 01:28:19,086
<i>♪ I will always be there for you ♪</i>

535
01:28:20,421 --> 01:28:25,592
<i>♪ Weya heya, heya heyo ♪♪</i>